{"parentUuid":"6fabac71-6620-4dc9-9577-afc1da094734","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"690dc5a9-089a-486a-a059-1e9b14cf6cd2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011ZvF6vRCThn6AituGnTwQC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Investigation Timeline: https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/1054\n2\t\n3\tThis file is the chronological log of multi-agent investigation for the report at\n4\t`/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/kiro-windows-bugs/docs/investigations/https-github-com-entireio-cli-issues-1054.md`. Each agent appends one entry per turn. Do not edit prior entries.\n5\t\n6\t## Round 1 / Turn 1 - claude-code\n7\t**Stance:** request-changes\n8\t**Date:** 2026-04-29T00:00:00Z\n9\t\n10\t### Changes\n11\t- Replaced the empty Symptom/Reproducer sections with the four concrete Windows symptoms reported by @sameerkhandisney in the issue thread, plus a static reproducer (`entire enable kiro` and inspecting the generated artifacts) and a note that the Windows-only stdin behavior cannot be reproduced on macOS/Linux.\n12\t- Added six numbered findings to the Investigation Trail with file:line evidence:\n13\t  - F1: `agents/entire-agent-kiro/internal/kiro/hooks.go:25-28,373-380` — hook commands hardcoded to `sh -c '... </dev/null'`, with `allHooksInstalled` (L233-249) and `allIDEHooksPresent` (L260-277) re-overwriting any manual Windows patch.\n14\t  - F2: `types.go:13-20` and `hooks.go:46-109,438-445,455-458` — hook payload struct has no session/conversation-ID field, and the cached UUID is wiped on every `stop`, so consecutive turns in the same Kiro chat tab split into separate entire sessions.\n15\t  - F3: `transcript.go:388-422` — `kiroDataDir` and `kiroExtensionStorageDir` only branch on `darwin`/default-Linux, so Windows falls through to non-existent XDG paths and every CLI/IDE/exec-log lookup fails through to `createPlaceholderTranscript` writing `{}`.\n16\t  - F4: `transcript.go:19-21` — `runSQLiteCommand` requires `sqlite3` on PATH, whic