{"parentUuid":"498fdec3-7645-4d29-8088-20545001c4b2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WGodxScmxahExp8onkA8gU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hooks unblocked = symptom #1 and #4 are fixed. Two bugs left to verify:\n\n## Bug #2: session grouping (multi-turn → one entire session)\n\n```powershell\n# In your test repo, send 3 prompts in the SAME Kiro chat tab.\n# After each one, dump the cached session id:\ntype .entire\\tmp\\kiro-active-session\n# expect: same value all 3 times — and persists across each agentStop, not deleted\n\n# List entire sessions and confirm all 3 turns map to ONE session\nentire sessions\n# expect: one session with 3 prompts, NOT 3 separate sessions\n```\n\nIf you see the cached session id change between turns or get deleted after stop, the session-resolver fix is misbehaving on your Windows install.\n\n## Bug #3: assistant responses captured (not just user prompts)\n\n```powershell\n# After a stop event, find the cached transcript and inspect it\ndir .entire\\tmp\\*.json\ntype .entire\\tmp\\<the-session-id>.json\n```\n\nWhat to look for:\n- Not just `{}` (placeholder = transcript capture failed)\n- `history` array with both `user` and `assistant` entries\n- Tool calls / file modifications under assistant entries (means execution-log enrichment from `%APPDATA%\\Kiro\\User\\globalStorage\\kiro.kiroagent\\...` worked)\n\nIf it's `{}`: Windows path resolution is wrong on your machine. Check:\n\n```powershell\ndir \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\kiro-cli\\data.sqlite3\"\ndir \"$env:APPDATA\\Kiro\\User\\globalStorage\\kiro.kiroagent\\workspace-sessions\"\n```\n\nBoth should exist. The agent assumes those paths.\n\n## Bug #4 (empty hook stdin)\n\nThere's no fix for \"Kiro doesn't send stdin payload\" — we sidestepped it by reading the IDE session files from disk. So **#4 passes automatically if #2 and #3 pass**.\n\n---\n\n## Quick all-in-one sanity script\n\n```powershell\n# After 3 prompts + a stop, run this from the test repo\n\"=== cached session id ===\"\ntype .entire\\tmp\\kiro-active-session\n\"=== cached transcripts ===\"\ndir .entire\\tmp\\*.json | Select-Object Name, Length\n\"=== entire sessions ===\"\nentire sessions\n\"=== kiro storage paths ===\"\ndir \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\kiro-cli\\data.sqlite3\"\ndir \"$env:APPDATA\\Kiro\\User\\globalStorage\\kiro.kiroagent\\workspace-sessions\"\n```\n\nPaste me the output and I can read whether #2 and #3 actually landed."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":767,"cache_read_input_tokens":228013,"output_tokens":1685,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":767,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1685,"cache_read_input_tokens":228013,"cache_creation_input_tokens":767,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":767},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CampKrgt3oLywVVmu4Pz8","type":"assistant","uuid":"83cc6e30-18c3-473c-9399-c0742e7ea95b","timestamp":"2026-05-06T18:50:18.698Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/kiro-windows-bugs","sessionId":"4369d6d2-a8cb-49ec-9554-6158e4c7e173","version":"2.1.131","gitBranch":"kiro-windows-bugs"}
