{"parentUuid":"af72c55e-56ac-4940-97ff-020e234930f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DeNT6aNzyrZs4m66ewR8vj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — this is platform-independent behavior. The transcript pairing and trim logic runs identically on macOS and Windows; the only Windows-specific code in my fix is the path-normalization helper. Whatever you're seeing in this output, you'd see the same on Mac.\n\nTwo things in the agent contribute to those orphan entries:\n\n**1. `convertIDETranscript` walks IDE entries in order.** If a Kiro IDE session has any non-strict-alternation (e.g., assistant entry without a preceding user, or trailing user with no assistant), the converter emits `{user=nil, assistant=X}` or `{user=X, assistant=nil}` paired entries. That's by design, not Windows.\n\n**2. `trimTranscriptHistory` cuts cumulative IDE history based on a stored offset.** Each stop event records `Position = len(history)`. The next stop reads from disk, runs conversion (which may produce extra entries from exec-log enrichment that weren't in the original IDE history), then slices `History[prev.Position:]`.\n\nThe combination means: if turn N produces N paired entries on disk, we save offset=N. If turn N+1 fires and conversion now produces N+2 paired entries (because exec-log enrichment expanded one turn into multiple action-derived assistant entries), the slice `[N:]` keeps 2 entries — one of which can be an orphaned assistant from inside the previous boundary.\n\nSpecifically, look at `enrichIDETranscriptWithExecutionLogs` in `transcript.go:1069` — when a turn has multiple `say`/`create`/`edit` actions, it appends extra `assistantEntries[1:]` with no user. If trim lands inside that run, the leading orphan surfaces.\n\nSo yes: **macOS would show the same pattern under the same conditions** (multi-action turn straddling a stop boundary, or IDE session not strictly alternating). It's a pre-existing logic concern, not a Windows regression. The Mac unit tests in `transcript_test.go` exercise tighter, hand-crafted IDE fixtures that don't trigger this edge case, which is why it wasn't visible.\n\nWorth fixing eventually, but it's separable from the Windows-port work and applies to every platform."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6719,"cache_read_input_tokens":287703,"output_tokens":3330,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6719,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":3330,"cache_read_input_tokens":287703,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6719},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CamvWpp23BX2mFAdNnx5t","type":"assistant","uuid":"6a19a036-b4c6-465b-9b4f-1db25a52558f","timestamp":"2026-05-06T20:11:50.762Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/alisha/.marvin/worktrees/kiro-windows-bugs/agents/entire-agent-kiro","sessionId":"4369d6d2-a8cb-49ec-9554-6158e4c7e173","version":"2.1.131","gitBranch":"kiro-windows-bugs","slug":"parsed-pondering-pancake"}
