he CLI invokes the freshly-built binary so a clean Mac end-to-end test is possible.\n\n## Approach\n\nTwo single-shot fixes, both inside the user's existing setup. No code changes to this branch are required.\n\n### Fix 1 — Enable external-plugin discovery in the test repo\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/alisha/Projects/test-repos/kiroide\n\n# Add external_agents: true to the existing settings file (preserves enabled/telemetry).\n# Use jq for a safe in-place merge.\ntmp=$(mktemp)\njq '. + {external_agents: true}' .entire/settings.json > \"$tmp\" && mv \"$tmp\" .entire/settings.json\n\ncat .entire/settings.json\n# expect: {\"enabled\": true, \"telemetry\": false, \"external_agents\": true}\n```\n\nWhy repo-level instead of user-level (`~/.entire/app-settings.json`): keeps the change scoped to this test repo only, doesn't silently affect other projects.\n\n### Fix 2 — Make the freshly-built binary win the PATH lookup\n\nPick one (recommended option first):\n\n```bash\n# Option A (recommended): replace the stale ~/.local/bin binary with the fresh build.\n# Single source of truth, no PATH reordering required.\ncp /Users/alisha/go/bin/entire-agent-kiro /Users/alisha/.local/bin/entire-agent-kiro\nwhich entire-agent-kiro                             # confirm path\n/Users/alisha/.local/bin/entire-agent-kiro info | jq '{name, capabilities}' # confirm name=kiro and compact_transcript=true\n```\n\nOption B (alternative): set `GOBIN=~/.local/bin` in shell rc and re-run `go install` from the agent dir. Same end state, but adds a permanent env var.\n\nOption C (alternative): delete `~/.local/bin/entire-agent-kiro` so `~/go/bin` wins. Cleanest but only works if `~/go/bin` is actually on PATH — verify with `echo $PATH | tr ':' '\\n' | grep -E 'go/bin|.local/bin'`.\n\n### Critical files referenced (read-only — no edits)\n\n- `cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/external/discovery.go:31-37` — settings gate that's blocking discovery today\n- `cli/cmd/entire/cli/hooks_cmd.go:44-52` — where the \"unknown agent\" error originates after the gated discovery returns empty\n- `~/Projects/test-repos/kiroide/.entire/settings.json` — the file to update (Fix 1)\n- `~/.local/bin/entire-agent-kiro` — the stale binary to replace (Fix 2 option A)\n- `~/go/bin/entire-agent-kiro` — the fresh build to copy from (Fix 2 option A source)\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter applying both fixes, in `~/Projects/test-repos/kiroide`:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Re-run hook installation so .kiro/hooks/* and .vscode/settings.json\n#    are written by the fresh binary (with our marshalJSON cleanup, no\n#    behavioral diff vs old on macOS — same sh -c '...' shape).\nentire agent add kiro --force\n\n# 2. Confirm kiro now shows up in the CLI's view\nentire agent list                                    # expect a checkmark next to kiro\n\n# 3. Manually invoke the hook command Kiro IDE will run, with a closed stdin\nsh -c 'entire hooks kiro stop </dev/null'\necho \"exit: $?\"                                      # expect 0, no \"unknown agent\" error\n\n# 4. Open the test repo in Kiro IDE on Mac, send a prompt, let it complete.\n#    Then check that the cached transcript captured content (not '{}').\ntype .entire/tmp/kiro-active-session                 # (use cat on Mac)\nls -la .entire/tmp/*.json\ncat .entire/tmp/<that-session-id>.json | jq '.history | length'\n# expect: ≥ 1 (transcript has real history entries, not just '{}')\n```\n\nIf step 3 still errors with \"unknown agent\": double-check `external_agents` is in the merged settings (`entire status` may print resolved settings, or read the file back). If step 4 shows `{}`: the disk-path lookup failed even on Mac — which would be a real regression from this branch and warrants opening `transcript.go` to investigate.\n\n## Out of scope (for separate follow-up)\n\n- The `~/.entire/app-settings.json` plaintext `anthropic_api_key` exposure noted earlier — rotate when convenient.\n- The orphaned `{user=null, assistant=...}` entry pairing observed in the Windows transc